+/** HST Office document tabs, the entry points other modules need.
+
+    Documents keep their own task frame and top-level window. The windows of a tab group
+    share one geometry and only the active one is shown (the others are "parked", i.e.
+    hidden); a tab strip in every member switches between them. The implementation lives
+    in framework/source/services/documenttabgroup.cxx.
+*/
+namespace framework::DocumentTabs
+{
+/** Call right before a task frame's container window is made visible (and brought to
+    front) by code that knows it is about to do so, e.g. SfxFrame::Appear(). The frame
+    joins the tab group, takes over the group's position and size while still unmapped,
+    and the previously shown member is parked once the new one is visible.
+    No-op when tabs are disabled. */
+FWK_DLLPUBLIC void prepareShow(const css::uno::Reference<css::frame::XFrame>& xFrame);
+}
